Guest native compiler and filesystem integration, revision0.12

All implementation sources are original Zero. tools/integrate.zero composes
kernel source parts and tools/build.zero builds native targets. The guest
controller is portability/guest/kernel-commands.zero.part; filesystem service
states are fs/guest-service.zero.part. ABI.ztext specifies the current contract.

--app64 and --app32 emit ZEROAPP1 images with bounded memory streams and
independent4MiB arenas. The kernel loads an architecture-matched compiler,
Ezero frontend and packer from its1MiB compiler bundle. Native app slots are
159744 bytes, with the Ezero runtime prefix at962560 and body at966656.
The original compilers execute inside the VM; no host compiler translates
terminal commands. The source command limit is480 bytes including the command
name, and application terminal output is4095 bytes.

The8MiB workspace holds context0, filesystem descriptor256, continuations512
and608, source4096, Ezero package270336, initializer393216, combined Zero589824,
compiled image1048576 (capacity524288), output1572864, filesystem service stack
1703936 (81920 bytes), application stack2097152 through8388608.
Each program gets a fresh service continuation. It invokes the same kernel
ZeroFS/ext4/NTFS/Btrfs drivers used by terminal commands. No command strings
or host filesystem are used for guest file access.

Implemented file primitives: readfile, save, writefile (exclusive), create,
del, watch, search, go and disks. Root syntax is A:| through Z:|. Relative
paths use the current volume. watch(.) and go(.) use its root. Names and
content remain bounded by existing filesystem profiles: flat ASCII names
of1..31 bytes, ASCII file contents including TAB/LF/CR up to400 bytes; ZeroFS has eight
file slots. Search supports * and ? in the filename component. go changes
the active terminal volume even after the program returns.

File/list outputs are staged and copied only when the whole result fits.
Malformed requests, unsupported filesystem profiles and capacity errors
return unsigned-1. Mutations run the existing flush protocols. No automatic
formatting, partition changes or writes to unsupported volumes occur.

These apps cooperate and share kernel memory; they are not isolated user
processes. Unsafe stores and infinite loops remain possible. Generic foreign
program loading, nested directories, descriptor-based guest file APIs and
persistent executable images are outside this interface. host() remains0,
and host command-line argument APIs remain unavailable in a guest.

Current validation: verification/guest-files-0.12/report.ztext records280
passed terminal commands on the0.12 candidate. ZeroFS/service/Ztext checks
passed BIOS32/64 and UEFI32/64 with cold-restart persistence. Original ext4,
NTFS and Btrfs guest service checks passed both32-bit and64-bit BIOS paths.
Dirty/unsupported profiles refused all mutation APIs without changing any
byte of their private test volumes. User-owned disks were never attached.
The report records the tested ISO SHA256; later builds need their own smoke
verification. Historical0.10/0.11 evidence is not used to certify these changes.
